WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.164
A compound works at nanomolar concentration in a protected assay. The

00:00:05.164 --> 00:00:09.779
number is seductive, but a patient never receives an assay plate.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.324
Solubility, absorption, distribution, metabolism and clearance decide

00:00:20.324 --> 00:00:24.847
whether the required free concentration reaches the tissue.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.256
A high tissue or plasma concentration can conceal extensive binding.

00:00:35.256 --> 00:00:39.712
Free exposure at the site of action is the relevant question.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.029
Ask what dose achieves occupancy for long enough, and

00:00:49.029 --> 00:00:52.508
what happens elsewhere in the body at that same exposure.

00:00:57.258 --> 00:01:01.049
Potency cannot compensate indefinitely for

00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:04.840
permeability barriers, toxicity or infeasible pharmacokinetics.

00:01:09.925 --> 00:01:14.354
The argument is about choosing compounds that can deliver

00:01:14.354 --> 00:01:18.784
an effective unbound concentration, not applauding the smallest assay number.
